# Project maintenance

1. Start with `AGENTS.md`; then read the matching file in `docs/prompts/`.
2. Keep `index.html`, `assets/styles.css`, `assets/app.js`, and `data/questions.js` separate.
3. Never move or copy question records into `index.html`.
4. Preserve `file://` use without Service Worker and HTTPS/localhost PWA installation.
5. App runtime stays remote-network-free: no fetch, modules, CDN, remote font/image, or framework.
6. Only `service-worker.js` may intercept controlled same-origin GET requests; never third-party traffic.
7. Keep manifest start/scope relative and maintain local 192, 512, and maskable icons.
8. Keep IDs exactly 1..100, unique, ordered, and nonempty.
9. Keep source labels limited to `zhihu-archive` and `supplemented`.
10. IDs 73, 89, and 90 are supplemented; never relabel them as article content.
11. Regenerate `data/questions.js` through `scripts/build_questions.py`; do not hand-edit it.
12. Preserve v3 plus safe v2 and v1 migration, 2/8/20 XP, 100 XP levels, review list without stream reinjection, and 20-distinct-question study days.
13. Treat localStorage as per-device; import replaces only after confirmation, with no merge or cloud sync.
14. Preserve Space, 1/2/3, arrows, J, storage recovery, accessibility, reduced motion, and 320px.
15. Add a failing behavior test before changing JavaScript, Service Worker, or verifier behavior.
16. Never copy source downloads, secrets, personal data, terminal artifacts, or temporary files.
17. After any data or UI change, run:
    - `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v`
    - `node --test tests/test_app.js`
    - `python3 scripts/verify_project.py`
    - `node --check assets/app.js`
    - `node --check service-worker.js`
